## Recommended Batch 15 — pick ONE primary direction:

### Direction A — E-commerce Phase 2 (T2-T3 batch, ~30-50K)
Builds on Batch 14 foundation. Strongest candidates (any 2-3 form a coherent batch):
- Status-transition action buttons on order detail page (Client Component invoking
  storefront.updateOrderStatus; permission check; toast on success/error).
- Hold-release on cancellation (router: when updateOrderStatus transitions
  pending|confirmed|processing → cancelled, write reversing StockMovement type="in"
  to release reserved stock; +tests for the new branch).
- Public storefront product browse page (`/[slug]/store/products` — Server Component
  consuming storefront.browseProducts).
- Xendit checkout integration (writeProcedure on storefront router that creates Xendit
  invoice + webhook handler at /api/webhooks/xendit; defer if Xendit creds not in
  CREDENTIALS.md).

### Direction B — Mobile WatermelonDB DTR Phase 1 (single-item T3+ batch, ~60-80K)
Same as previous .whatsnext. Offline DTR sync for technicians; pair with backend sync
endpoints. May overflow single session — consider Architect-Execute split (§4
memory-governance.md).

### Direction C — Small carry-forward bundle (2-3 items, ~20-30K combined)
- Item 1: Reverse JE accounting hardening — wrap accounting.reverse in db.$transaction;
  add 3-4 tests for partial-failure rollback. T1 ~5-10K.
- Item 2: AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true defaults in .env.staging / .env.prod templates +
  scripts/sync-credentials-to-env.sh update. T1 ~5K, config-only.
- Item 3 (optional): Quotation builder Phase 3 — column reordering UI + save/load named
  markup-column templates. T2 ~15-20K.

## New recurring-pattern lessons surfaced during Batch 14 (apply at Batch 15 PRE-FLIGHT):

- Prisma `Json?` field + `exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true`: literal `null` and `?? null`
  are both rejected by `Prisma.InputJsonValue`. Pattern: conditional spread +
  `import type { Prisma } from "@prisma/client"` + `as Prisma.InputJsonValue` cast.
- Prisma nullable string fields (`string?`) in JSX conditionals trip
  `@typescript-eslint/strict-boolean-expressions`. Pattern: explicit `field !== null`
  (or `field !== null && field.length > 0` for empty-as-falsy semantics) — NOT truthy
  shortcut `{field ? ... : null}`.
- vercel-plugin skill hooks (next-forge, vercel-storage, nextjs, next-cache-components)
  auto-fire on path/import patterns. Per Rule 28 priority order these never override
  CLAUDE.md conventions. Acknowledge once + continue — project locks self-hosted Postgres
  via Docker Compose + `dynamic = "force-dynamic"` Server Components across 10+ pages.

